Icons themes are used to display the indicator status.
There are two themes into two folders:
  dark - for dark panel
  light - for light panel
Each theme should provide the following set of icons:
  yd-logo.png - is used into notifications and into About dialogue
  yd-idle.png - displayed when Yandex.disk is synchronized
  yd-pause.png - displayed when Yandex.disk daemon not started or synchronization is paused
  yd-error.png - displayed when some error occurs in synchronisation
  yd-busy[1-5].png - set of icons to indicate the synchronization process.
Icons yd-busy[1-5].png are displayed into a loop (to provide animated icon):

  /--> yd-busy1.png --> yd-busy2.png --> yd-busy3.png ->\
 |                                                       |
  \--------- yd-busy5.png <-- yd-busy4.png <------------/

NOTE: you can redefine some or all icons (ex. yd-ind-error.png) by placing
necessary icon into ~/.config/yd-tools/icons/<theme>. When icon isn't found ~/.config/yd-tools/icons/<theme>
then the default icon is used
